---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Be Insiculous — a small studio"
  description="Be Insiculous — a small studio: 2D games on our own Rust engine, and planning tools for ordinary life."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="section-label">a small studio</p>
    <h1>Be Insiculous</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A few of us, a Rust engine, and two kinds of thing: 2D games, and
      planning tools for ordinary life.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- The art-policy paragraph is quoted from docs/thesis.md, which is where that wording is
       maintained; it matches the sentence on /games/. Change it there first. -->
  <section>
    <h2>The games</h2>
    <p>
      Six arcade games so far, all in alpha, all running on
      <strong>Insiculous 2D</strong> — our own 2D engine, written in Rust.
      Each one is two-player, and each has an escalating <em>chaos mode</em>
      that bends the rules of the original. They are a run at the 20 Games
      Challenge: desktop builds today, browser versions when the engine's web
      export ships.
    </p>
    <p>
      The games listed on this site are free and use AI art. The games we sell
      carry none — those are made by our own artists, and they ship on Steam
      and the app stores rather than here.
    </p>
    <p>
      The engine pulls double duty: it runs the games, and it is a
      <a href="/engine/">proving ground for agentic coding tools</a> — real
      tasks on a live Rust codebase.
    </p>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER: add a paragraph on current focus (e.g. Deion the Insiculous / web export) when you're ready to talk about it publicly. -->
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The planner</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/fortknight/">FortKnight</a> and
      <a href="/forkknife/">ForkKnife</a> are two views of one planner.
      FortKnight is the schedule: a repeating fourteen-day cycle, a page per
      day, and where your time actually goes by category. ForkKnife is the
      menu: the meals, the dish for each day, and the prep and cooking tasks
      that come with them.
    </p>
    <p>
      It runs in your browser with no account and no server — your profile
      stays on your device. There is no AI in the app either: if you want help
      from an assistant, you download your files and take them to your own.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <a class="button" href="/games/">browse the games →</a>
    <a class="button" href="/fortknight/">open the planner →</a>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/devlog/">read the devlog →</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 2rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    max-width: 34em;
  }

  section p {
    max-width: 42em;
  }

  .cta {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* .button / .button.secondary now live in src/styles/global.css — the devlog uses them too. */
</style>
